      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Do not take 2000mg of potassium chloride at once, as it is a high dose that carries significant risks of serious heart arrhythmias, especially when you are dehydrated and already compromised. Before taking any supplement, you should sit down, drink plenty of water mixed with electrolytes, and consider reaching out to a medical professional immediately, as unexplained leg cramps during and after intense exercise can sometimes indicate an underlying condition like an electrolyte imbalance or other medical issues. It is much safer to seek personalized medical advice given your specific symptoms rather than self-medicing a potentially dangerous dose.",
